<title>BELGIUM: Belgian state notes raised total 8.0 bln bfr.</title>
<headline>Belgian state notes raised total 8.0 bln bfr.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian Finance Ministry said on Wednesday an issue of two types of state notes had raised a total 8.00 billion Belgian francs by the end of the subscription period.</p>
<p>The ministry said in a statement that altogether it had sold 5.65 billion francs of five-year notes, extendable to seven years. The notes carry a fixed coupon of 4.70 percent.</p>
<p>Notes with revisable coupons and put options after three, five and seven years raised 2.35 billion francs.</p>
<p>Subscriptions closed on Tuesday.</p>
